[
    {
        "content": "<p>Why is <code>Polynomial.rootSet</code> a <code>Set</code> rather than a <code>Finset</code>? It's defined in terms of <code>Polynomial.roots</code>, which is the empty set when the polynomial is constant (although strangely the lemma says it's <code>0</code> rather than the empty set), so it's always finite anyway. Is it worth making the change to a <code>Finset</code>? My impression is that it's easier to go from a <code>Finset</code> to a <code>Set</code> so the definition as a <code>Finset</code> is better.</p>",
        "id": 585987470,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776370103
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there precedent for naming something <code>...Set</code> when it's a <code>Finset</code>, or would this have to be called <code>rootFinset</code>?</p>",
        "id": 585989810,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776371001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Possibly, given that there's <code>Polynomial.nthRootsFinset</code>, but I do not mind this change</p>",
        "id": 585989950,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776371063
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also since we're on the subject, I'd love to have <code>arootSet S</code> and remove the parameter of <code>rootSet</code> (so it can use <code>roots</code> and not <code>aroots</code>)</p>",
        "id": 585990063,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776371107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes! That would also be lovely (possibly also with the renaming into <code>arootFinset</code>)</p>",
        "id": 585990101,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776371127
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ooh and maybe after the <code>Finset</code> rename we can define <code>p.rootSet := setOf p.IsRoot</code>, to get access to the root set even for non-domains</p>",
        "id": 585990361,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776371225
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So you propose we keep the name <code>rootSet</code> for <code>setOf p.IsRoot</code> and have another <code>rootFinset</code>?</p>",
        "id": 585990490,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776371289
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is likely a mix of historical mistakes and strange decisions made when the library was very young. Anything that improves the current mess is surely welcome, but it's maybe better to go one step at a time (unless this means repeating painful refactors).</p>",
        "id": 585995579,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776373592
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wait, there are non-constant polynomials with infinitely many roots!</p>",
        "id": 585996064,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776373787
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In domains?</p>",
        "id": 585996239,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776373848
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No of course not in domains (commutative)</p>",
        "id": 585996422,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776373917
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So what's the issue?<br>\nWe currently have:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">rootSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and the changes suggested so far are to have:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">rootSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"n\">arootSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rootFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"n\">arootFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Also there are these multisets, which can remain as they are:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">roots</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"n\">aroots</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585996979,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776374144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Polynomial.2ErootSet.20as.20a.20Finset/near/585996064\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wait, there are non-constant polynomials with infinitely many roots!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Polynomial.rootSet#doc\">docs#Polynomial.rootSet</a> asssumes <code>IsDomain</code> for the target.</p>",
        "id": 585997216,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1776374251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah ok, then it should be a finset, I agree.</p>",
        "id": 585999725,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776375601
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Polynomial.2ErootSet.20as.20a.20Finset/near/585996422\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No of course not in domains (commutative)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><del>Zero?</del> Oh non-constant, I read constant</p>",
        "id": 586002116,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776376990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My logic is that since we're just changing the definition and not renaming it, we don't need 100 deprecations, but then again we need 100 API lemmas...</p>",
        "id": 586002610,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776377232
    }
